  "configuration_id": "config_006",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_018 (rna_only, multiprofile, scgpt, avgpool) at 0.5305 acc / 0.5152 F1, which surprisingly outperforms the best multimodal setup (config_009, 0.5176). This suggests the RNA representation is the dominant signal, yet we have only tested one RNA encoder (scgpt). Uncertainty: We have zero evidence on whether scvi_n200 or pca_n2000 would improve upon scgpt in the multiprofile setting. This experiment tests the RNA encoder choice in isolation (only rna_encoder changes from config_018), keeping the best-known profile setting (multiprofile) and aggregation (avgpool) fixed. If scvi_n200 exceeds scgpt, it reveals a better representation and opens a new search direction; if it underperforms, it confirms scgpt as the preferred encoder and lets us redirect budget toward fusion or image-encoder questions. Under a limited budget, resolving the RNA encoder question is more informative than re-testing aggregation (which already has moderate evidence favoring avgpool) because the RNA encoder is the primary signal in the top-performing model and remains completely unexplored."
}

